diff --git a/docs/chat-bots.md b/docs/chat-bots.md
index e9d7f09..3e87dd4 100644
--- a/docs/chat-bots.md
+++ b/docs/chat-bots.md
@@ -23,3 +23,45 @@ Treat the bot code like a password. Keep it in your secret store, use HTTPS,
 and don't print the request URL in shell traces or CI logs. Campfire filters the
 code from its normal request logs, but any reverse proxy or access log in front
 of Campfire must also redact the code segment (or omit these paths).
+
+## Receiving mentions
+
+Set **Webhook URL** when creating or editing your bot. Clear the field and save
+to turn delivery off. Use a publicly reachable HTTP(S) URL, preferably HTTPS.
+Campfire does not send webhooks to private network addresses or follow redirects.
+
+Select the bot from the `@` autocomplete in a room where it is a member. When a
+person posts the message, Campfire queues one callback per mentioned bot, even
+if it was mentioned more than once. Delivery runs in the background, so the
+sender does not wait for the webhook. Editing a message or posting as a bot does
+not trigger a callback.
+
+Campfire sends an HTTP `POST` with `Content-Type: application/json`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "event": "mention",
+  "author": { "id": 7, "name": "Alice" },
+  "room": { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/42-Xy3abc9defGh/messages" },
+  "message": {
+    "id": 118,
+    "body": {
+      "text": "restart the build please",
+      "html": "<div>… full rich-text body …</div>"
+    },
+    "link": "/rooms/5/@118"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`body.text` omits the receiving bot's mentions; `body.html` contains the original
+rich-text markup, including mentions. Treat both as user input. `message.link`
+opens the room at the message for a signed-in room member. Both URL paths are
+relative to your Campfire origin. In particular, `room.reply_to` contains the
+bot's code: keep it private, just as you would the code itself.
+
+To reply immediately, return `200 OK` with `Content-Type: text/plain` or
+`text/html` and the message as the response body. Return `204 No Content` to
+skip the immediate reply. To reply later, append `room.reply_to` to your
+Campfire origin and post UTF-8 text as described above. Webhook requests time
+out after 10 seconds, and response bodies larger than 1 MiB are ignored.
